@* The privacy policy, as it was on the old ravenhosting.cloud, and what the site's own traffic counts keep (Analytics) *@
<SitePage Title="Privacy Policy">
    <div class="prose">
        <p>
            Take part in the journey to reclaim the internet where knowledge, privacy, and true social connections
            thrive.
        </p>
        <p>
            Raven hosting is a non-profit, open-source project, focused on safeguarding human rights in the digital
            age. Our mission is to empower individuals with the ability to establish their unique online identities,
            each anchored by its own domain name and certificate. Raven hosting is both completely decentralized and
            integrates seamlessly with existing Internet technologies, allowing users to host their own web pages,
            post blogs, engage in social networking, and use services like true peer-to-peer chat clients and
            personal image libraries.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our commitment to decentralized user control over personal data and online privacy is uncompromising. As
            part of this commitment, we employ zero-knowledge encryption. This means that user data is not just
            encrypted but is structured in such a way that only the user can decrypt and access their information -
            even Raven hosting cannot access this data.
        </p>
        <p>
            We aim to pioneer a new era of a decentralized internet, one where knowledge, privacy, and genuine social
            connections are paramount.
        </p>
        <h2>Visits to this site</h2>
        <p>
            We count visits to this site ourselves, without cookies or third-party services. For each page request we
            record the page, the referring site, the device type, and a daily-changing anonymous visitor code derived
            from your IP address and browser; we do not store your IP address. We do this to understand how the site
            is used (legitimate interest). Individual records are deleted after 90 days; only daily totals are kept.
        </p>
    </div>
</SitePage>
